1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Modori is a local desktop research workflow for making a limited set of statistical choices visible before calculation.

2
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:27,000
This was an existing project. During Build Week, I used Codex with GPT-5.6 to revise the Windows research surface, extend deterministic clarification and passport authority, add a variable-meaning review, and harden release evidence.

3
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:39,000
GPT-5.6 was a build-time engineering collaborator, not a runtime model. I retained the product, licensing, claim, hardware, and release decisions.

4
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:55,000
I select English and Casual Mode, then open a deterministic synthetic file with stress and sleep hours. It contains no real respondent records.

5
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Modori previews the table before import. Source cells are read-only; transformations become recorded steps and new variables. The current runtime has no configured hosted analysis, network client, or telemetry route.

6
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:34,000
Research OS P1 supports exactly six bounded tasks. I accept the noncausal boundary, choose linear co-movement, and draft both variable roles for this exact dataset.

7
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:49,000
Before any durable request is created, the Variable Meaning Gate shows the current labels, measurement levels, missing codes, and any definition or unit that is not recorded.

8
00:01:49,000 --> 00:02:07,000
After I confirm those meanings, bounded clarification records my answers. A deterministic policy can explain its question order, and the AnalysisPassport stays bound to the data and decision state.

9
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:29,000
The Pearson candidate is experimental, not an accuracy ranking, and cannot run automatically. I review and confirm its exact configuration; confirmation adds no result and the separate Run action is now available.

10
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:44,000
Only Run starts the calculation. For this synthetic file, Modori reports an association of negative point nine nine five across sixteen rows, not a causal conclusion or validated recommendation.

11
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:55,000
I save this English report locally after Run. This bounded walkthrough does not establish full bilingual coverage or recommendation validity.
